-   Maintain Excel soft copy of Bond register Issue VAT Challan 6.1, 6.2, 6.3 and submit monthly VAT return (9.1);

-   Must have ability to manage any task through excellent coordination between government and private authorities and organizations in Bangladesh;

-   Must have experience in obtaining all types of Licenses renewal for Woven Garments/Washing Factory;

-   Obtain/renewal and maintain BOILER licenses with regulations and timely;

-   Maintaining effective liaison with DOT, SIDA, BEPZA, EPB, NBR, Customs Bond, Customs;

-   Excise and VAT, 801, DEDO, CCl&E, Narcotic, NSI, SB, and other government offices;

-   Capable on matters such as Bill of Entry, Customs SRO, HS Code, Customs Act, Import Export;

-   Policy, In-Bond and Ex-Bond, and Customs Annual Audit;

-   Manage regulatory communications during crises and coordinate with internal management and staff;

-   To work in coordination with all applicable laws and regulations related to the import and export process;

-   Organize and present necessary reports to both internal and external stakeholders;

-   Perform any other tasks assigned by management; Oversee and manage customs bonds to ensure compliance with regulations ant timely renewals;

-   Supervising and guiding effectively of a group of operational teams in the related field;

-   Overall follow-up in all Customs & Govt. Compliance matters for smooth running of 3 large woven garment industries and 1 large washing plant.

**Company Overview:** China Harbour Engineering Company Ltd. (CHEC) is a world-renowned international contractor and a subsidiary of China Communications Construction Company Ltd. (CCCC), a Global Fortune 500 enterprise. CHEC operates through more than 90 branches across over 100 countries and regions, employing more than 15,000 professionals worldwide. The company manages projects valued at over USD 20 billion, with an annual turnover exceeding USD 9 billion. CHEC is a global leader in large-scale infrastructure development with over 45 years of proven experience in delivering complex engineering projects. Its core expertise includes ports and harbour development, marine structures, capital and maintenance dredging, mass rapid transit (MRT) systems, roads and bridges, railways, airports, and industrial plant construction. The company is committed to providing comprehensive, end-to-end solutions to its clients. Leveraging its extensive international engineering experience, global business network, highly skilled management team, and strong financial capacity, CHEC delivers a wide range of project delivery models, including Design & Build (D&B), Engineering, Procurement and Construction (EPC), Project Management Consultancy (PMC), Build-Transfer (BT) and Build-Operate-Transfer (BOT).

China Harbour Engineering Company Ltd. (Bangladesh Branch) is seeking a highly experienced Civil Engineer for the role of **Tender Engineer-Cost & Commercial**.

**Job Responsibilities**:

-   Reviewing and analyzing technical specifications, drawings and employer requirements to determine material quantities and project scope;
-   Preparing **Quantity Take-Offs (QTO)** and verifying material quantities from engineering drawings for accurate cost estimation;
-   Preparing and reviewing **Bills of Quantities (BOQ)** in accordance with project drawings and specifications;
-   Monitoring and analyzing construction market prices, material cost trends, and rate fluctuations through market research and industry benchmarking to ensure accurate cost estimation;
-   Identifying, evaluating and developing reliable vendors, suppliers and subcontractors by conducting market surveys and site visits, as required, to expand the supplier network, verify capabilities and establish long-term professional relationships that support competitive tendering;
-   Preparing and issuing **Requests for Quotations (RFQs)** based on project requisitions and specifications;
-   Performing detailed cost estimation and budget preparation, ensuring alignment with project scope and financial objectives;
-   Collecting quotations from multiple vendors, subcontractors, and suppliers and preparing **Comparative Statements (CS)** for cost analysis and decision-making;
-   Supporting tender preparation and submission by ensuring accurate cost data, complete documentation, timely submissions and strategic input for competitive bidding.

-   Oversee daily, weekly, and monthly reconciliation of all bank accounts and cash books to ensure financial accuracy and compliance;

-   Formulate, implement, and regularly update financial policies, protocols, and Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) in alignment with company goals;

-   Supervise and guide the Accounts & Finance team to ensure efficient, error-free day-to-day operations;

-   Supervise monthly TDS and VDS calculations for subcontractor/vendor payments and ensure timely submission of regulatory reports;

-   Provide leadership in audit preparation, financial reporting, and budgetary control; coordinate internal and external audits.

-   Supervise vendor payments, accounts payable, and procurement bills;

-   . Monitor customer billing, accounts receivable, and collections;

-   Prepare financial statements, budgets, and forecasts;

-   Ensure timely and accurate reporting of financial information;

-   Maintain compliance with local laws, tax regulations, and corporate policies;

-   Monitor cash flow, cost control, and financial planning;

-   Coordinate with auditors, banks, and regulatory authorities.

-   Conducting classes following the university guidelines;
-   Counseling students;
-   Conducting extra-curricular activities;
-   Arranging workshop, seminar, conference, symposium etc.;
-   Contributing towards the development of the Department as well as of the University;
-   Conducting research and publishing;
-   Other responsibilities as assigned by the Department and the School;

**Job description:** The responsibilities of the Head of Finance and Accounts will be the followings but not limited to these:

-   Overall responsibility for preparation of financial statements and weekly/monthly management reports for decision making;

-   Ensure maintenance of proper books of account and records and preserve those appropriately;

-   Preparation of reconciliation statements, tax and VAT planning and annual/monthly returns for submission to the relevant authority;

-   Take the lead of overall financial management of Vision Care Foundation and BEHRI;

-   Work with the senior management in preparing financial planning, develop and implement internal control system and ensure all types regulatory compliances;

-   Analyze revenue earnings opportunities and economic trends and identify areas for cost reduction and process enhancement;

-   Manage business through required analysis and evaluate & manage fund structure and fundraising initiatives;

-   Evaluate business performance with tracking tools, establish corrective measures as may be needed and prepare detailed reports for decision making;

-   Lead and develop the finance personnel, oversee the accounting software, ensure data integrity and audit trial in accounting software;

-   Ensure proper and timely cooperation with the regulators, stakeholders, internal & external auditors.

**Pretty Group**, one of the largest export-oriented Group of Companies in Bangladesh, is looking for a highly experienced **General Manager (Corporate HR)**.

This position is based in the **Corporate Head Office, Gulshan - 02, Dhaka - 1212.**

The Incumbent will be responsible to successfully carry out the **Corporate Core HR Functions**; the execution of all People Processes and a Key Contributor in Developing, Managing & Implementing HR Strategies, Programs & Guidelines across all **Core HR areas including Talent Management, Organization Development, Training & Development, Policy & Procedure and so on.**

**Job Responsibilities**

-   Develop and administrate full spectrum of Core HR Functions which includes Manpower Planning, Talent Acquisition, Performance Management, Employee Relations, Compensation & Benefits aligned with the overall business strategy;

-   Lead a Team of HR Professionals; provide coaching, mentoring and be an inspirational leader to support all relevant Core HR Functions for the whole Group;

-   Formulate and implement HR strategies in line with business strategies to attain the goal of the organization;

-   Prepare Annual HR Budget and manage HR activity to ensure costs are within the Budget;

-   Ensure effective talent acquisition, orientation, induction, learning and development program across the groups;

-   Acting as a focal point of Organization Development (OD) and overseeing the development of employee career path;

-   Manage all HR processes and change management in line with Group HR practices suitable for organizational context;

-   Maintain liaison with other departments in connection with streamlining Core HR practices;

-   Develop, formulate and implement various Policies and Procedures;

-   Ensure appropriate reward and recognition as well as engagement program to ensure optimum employee engagement level;

-   Formulate career development plans & proper succession planning for the group;

-   Develop HR Analytics and HR Audit for the whole Group;

-   Any other assignment as assigned by the top management.
